<title>SWITZERLAND: Hero plans two divestitures - report.</title>
<headline>Hero plans two divestitures - report.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss food company Hero is on the verge of selling two industrial baking operations, chief executive Lutz Peters was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>The Finanz und Wirtschaft newspaper quoted him as saying Hero &quot;was now in the process&quot; of selling U.S. operation Best Brands, with $110 million in sales, and Britain's Rayner, with 20 million pounds in turnover.</p>
<p>He did not say to whom the businesses might be sold, and no one was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Proceeds could help cut debt at Hero, which is controlled by Germany's Schwartau Group.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
